"help.flow.title" = "How reverse singing works";
"help.flow.sing" = "Sing";
"help.flow.flip" = "Flip";
"help.flow.copy" = "Copy";
"help.flow.flipBack" = "Flip back";
"help.flow.caption" = "Sing a line and hear it backwards. Copy that nonsense as closely as you can, then flip your copy around. Nail it, and out comes the song.";
"help.gettingStarted.1.q" = "What is Dubloon?";
"help.gettingStarted.1.a" = "Four voice games that need nothing but your microphone. Reverse Singing: sing a song backwards. Movie Scene Dub: put your voice into a film scene, line by line. Home Video Dub: put your voice on a video you've filmed. Sound Imitation: copy a sound and get a verdict. Pick one from the menu.";
"help.gettingStarted.2.q" = "Which games are free?";
"help.gettingStarted.2.a" = "Reverse Singing and Home Video Dub are free, for as long as you like. Movie Scene Dub and Sound Imitation come with Dubloon Pro, along with Booth Cam.";
"help.gettingStarted.3.q" = "Do I need headphones?";
"help.gettingStarted.3.a" = "No, but they help when you dub. With headphones on, you can hear the original line while you record (switch on Original in Headphones in Settings). Through the speaker it would end up in your take, so Dubloon only plays it in headphones. Wired headphones keep the timing tightest: Bluetooth adds a small delay.";
"help.reverse.1.q" = "How does reverse singing work?";
"help.reverse.1.a" = "Tap Record Audio and sing a line of a song. Play Backwards to hear it reversed. Then tap Sing It Back and copy that backwards sound as closely as you can. Dubloon flips your copy around, and if you got it right you hear the song again, in your voice.";
"help.reverse.2.q" = "What do the four play buttons do?";
"help.reverse.2.a" = "Original is the line you sang. Reversed is that line backwards, the sound to copy. Your Take is your copy as you sang it. Your Take, Reversed is your copy flipped back around: the one that should sound like the song.";
"help.reverse.3.q" = "How is my score worked out?";
"help.reverse.3.a" = "Dubloon compares your take, flipped back, with your original line: where the sound rises and falls, and how the rhythm lines up. It all happens on your device. Short lines with clear words score best; go for the rhythm first and the vowels second.";
"help.reverse.4.q" = "Simple or Complex?";
"help.reverse.4.a" = "Two looks for the same game, switched from the options button at the top of the screen. Simple is big buttons and nothing to trip over. Complex adds the waveform and Audio Controls: loop, speed and pitch. Slowing the reversed line down is the best way to learn it.";
"help.reverse.5.q" = "Where are my saved sessions?";
"help.reverse.5.a" = "Tap the archive button at the top of the Reverse Singing screen. Starting a new session puts the current one in the archive, so nothing is thrown away. Swipe a session in the archive to delete it.";
"help.dub.1.q" = "How do I dub a scene?";
"help.dub.1.a" = "Open Movie Scene Dub and pick a scene, then tap Start Dubbing. For each line, listen to the original, then press record: you get three beats of count-in, and the mic closes by itself when the line ends. Move on with Next, and come back to any line whenever you like.";
"help.dub.2.q" = "What does the pacing bar mean?";
"help.dub.2.a" = "It shows how long the original line runs. It turns amber the moment you run past it, so you know to speed up. Under your take, the original's waveform shows where you came in early, rushed or left a gap.";
"help.dub.3.q" = "How are dubs scored?";
"help.dub.3.a" = "Each take is marked on timing (did you start and stop with the original), pacing (did you keep its rhythm) and delivery (did your loud and quiet parts follow it). The scene gets a score too, with your best line and the one worth another go. Don't want to be judged? Turn off Score my takes in the dub options.";
"help.dub.4.q" = "How do I hear myself in the film?";
"help.dub.4.a" = "Tap Play My Dub on the scene. Your takes drop into the film in place of the original lines; anything you haven't dubbed yet plays as it was. Watch Original plays the scene untouched.";
"help.homeVideo.1.q" = "How do I dub my own video?";
"help.homeVideo.1.a" = "Tap the empty picture and choose a video from your library, up to a minute long. Press record: after the count-in the video plays from the start and your voice goes on top. When it ends your version plays, ready to share or record again.";
"help.homeVideo.2.q" = "How do I time my sounds?";
"help.homeVideo.2.a" = "The wave under the picture is the video's own sound, and the line moving across it is where the video is. Watch it to land a bark or a laugh at the right moment. After a take, your voice is drawn over it in red.";
"help.homeVideo.3.q" = "Can I hear the video while I record?";
"help.homeVideo.3.a" = "Yes, with headphones on. Through the speaker the video plays silently, so its sound doesn't end up in your take. Keep the original sound puts it back, quietly, under your voice in the finished video.";
"help.booth.1.q" = "What is Booth Cam?";
"help.booth.1.a" = "Booth Cam films your face with the front camera while you perform, so the reaction can go into the video with the dub. It's off until you turn it on with the camera key on the recording screen or in Settings. The footage stays on your device.";
"help.booth.2.q" = "How do I export a video?";
"help.booth.2.a" = "Tap Export Video on a scene. Choose the cut (the full scene, or a session reel of just the lines you dubbed) and where your booth footage goes: in the corner, stacked for a story, as a reaction, or side by side. Before it renders, Dubloon shows whose scene it is, so you can keep the credit when you share.";
"help.booth.3.q" = "How do I delete booth footage?";
"help.booth.3.a" = "Settings shows how much space booth footage uses, with a button to delete all booth takes. Your voice takes and your dubs stay. Deleting a scene also deletes its takes and footage.";
"help.packs.1.q" = "How do I add more scenes?";
"help.packs.1.a" = "Scenes come as dub packs: a folder, or a .zip, .7z or .rar archive. Tap + in Movie Scene Dub and pick one from Files, or send it to Dubloon from AirDrop or any share sheet. Dubloon unpacks it and the scene appears in the list.";
"help.packs.2.q" = "Where do dub packs come from?";
"help.packs.2.a" = "Two scenes come with the app. Every other pack is made and shared by other players; Dubloon doesn't include, host or sell any films. Only dub what you have the right to use, and follow the copyright rules where you live.";
"help.packs.3.q" = "A pack won't import. What now?";
"help.packs.3.a" = "Dubloon says what went wrong. The usual fixes: if the file is in iCloud, open it in Files first so it downloads. If the archive has a password, ask its maker for one without. If it won't unpack, re-save it as a .zip. And if Dubloon says it isn't a dub pack, it needs a text file and a recording for every line.";
"help.imitate.1.q" = "How does Sound Imitation work?";
"help.imitate.1.a" = "Pick a sound, tap Hear it, then tap Imitate and make the sound yourself. Dubloon compares your attempt with the real thing and stamps a verdict on it. Your best score for each sound is kept, so you can come back and beat it.";
"help.imitate.2.q" = "What gets judged?";
"help.imitate.2.a" = "Four things: rhythm (the rise and fall of the sound over time), pitch, tone (bright or dull) and length. Listen a couple of times first, match the length, then worry about the pitch.";
"help.imitate.3.q" = "Can I share an attempt?";
"help.imitate.3.a" = "Yes. After a verdict, tap Make video: the sound, your attempt and your score, ready to send. With Booth Cam on, your face is in it too.";
"help.pro.1.q" = "What does Dubloon Pro unlock?";
"help.pro.1.a" = "Movie Scene Dub with every scene and community pack, Sound Imitation, Booth Cam and video exports. Reverse Singing is free either way. Pro is a one-time purchase or a subscription, and it unlocks on your iPhone and your Mac with the same Apple Account.";
"help.pro.2.q" = "I bought Pro, but it's locked.";
"help.pro.2.a" = "Open Settings and tap Restore purchase. Make sure you're signed in to the App Store with the Apple Account you bought it with. On a new phone or after reinstalling, restoring brings it back at no cost.";
"help.pro.3.q" = "How do I cancel or change my subscription?";
"help.pro.3.a" = "In Settings, tap Manage subscription. You can also do it in the Settings app: tap your name, then Subscriptions. Cancel at least 24 hours before it renews and you keep Pro until the end of the period you paid for. Refunds are handled by Apple.";
"help.privacy.1.q" = "Are my recordings uploaded anywhere?";
"help.privacy.1.a" = "No. Your recordings, takes, booth footage and videos stay on your device until you choose to share them. Scoring happens on your device too. There is no account and nothing to sign up for.";
"help.privacy.2.q" = "What does Dubloon collect?";
"help.privacy.2.a" = "Anonymous usage statistics and crash reports, which help find bugs and decide what to build next: things like which game was opened and what score came out, never the sound of a recording. Turn it off in Settings with Share usage data. The Privacy Policy has every detail.";
"help.troubleshooting.1.q" = "Dubloon can't hear me.";
"help.troubleshooting.1.a" = "Check that Dubloon may use the microphone: in the Settings app, open Dubloon and switch on Microphone. If another app is using the audio, such as a call, end it and try again.";
"help.troubleshooting.2.q" = "I can't hear anything.";
"help.troubleshooting.2.a" = "Turn the volume up, and check whether Bluetooth headphones or a speaker have connected somewhere else. The original line during recording only plays in headphones, on purpose, so it stays out of your take.";
"help.troubleshooting.3.q" = "My dub is out of sync with the picture.";
"help.troubleshooting.3.a" = "Bluetooth headphones add a delay, so you hear the original a little late and come in late. Wired headphones, or none, fix it. If Dubloon says a scene's video runs ahead of the voices, import that pack again.";
"help.troubleshooting.4.q" = "Booth Cam won't turn on.";
"help.troubleshooting.4.a" = "Dubloon needs the camera for it. In the Settings app, open Dubloon and switch on Camera. Booth Cam is part of Dubloon Pro.";
